.TH MODBUS-CACHE-CTL 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.4.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
modbus-cache-ctl \- one-shot control client for the modbus-cache daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modbus-cache-ctl
.RI [ options ]
.IB command " [args ...]"
.br
.B modbus-cache-ctl
.RI [ options ]
< commands

.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends one control command (or a batch piped on stdin, one per line) to the
\fBmodbus-cache\fR JSON-lines control server and prints the replies on
stdout, one per line. Every invocation lands in the audit trail (prefix
\fBCTL\fR).
.PP
The command grammar is the daemon's: \fBset\fR/\fBunset\fR/\fBshow\fR/
\fBhelp\fR (the settings registry), \fBinspect\fR,
\fBshow connections\fR, \fBshow cache\fR [\fBall\fR],
\fBshow write registers profile\fR, \fBshow uplink\fR,
\fBshow version\fR, \fBshow knobs\fR (the dictionary of the registry),
\fBrequest flush cache\fR, \fBrequest reload\fR, \fBrequest restart\fR,
\fBshutdown\fR,
\fBquit\fR. See
.BR modbus-cache (1)
CONTROL.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-control\-port
control server target: unix socket path or TCP port on 127.0.0.1,
auto\-detected (env CTL when unset) — same flag as the proxy itself
.TP
.B command
control command, e.g. inspect, show config, show cache, request clear
cache, request reload\-config, request restart, shutdown
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " N"
socket timeout in seconds
.TP
.B \-\-control\-token
control auth token for TCP (env CONTROL_TOKEN); a file:<path> value
reads the first line of an owner\-only 0600 file
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-log
audit trail: a file path, \- for stdout, or none for no local file (the
forward carries the trail); the XDG state home when unset
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-forward
also forward every audit line: none, syslog, syslog:/path,
udp://host[:port] or tcp://host[:port] (the off\-box copy,
docs/AUDIT.md)
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-forward\-format
the remote forward's envelope: rfc5424 (the default) or cef — the local
syslog forms keep the verbatim send
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-max\-mb " N"
rotate the audit log at this size, 0 = off
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-files " N"
rotated audit backups to keep
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audit\-log
disable the audit trail


.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B modbus-cache-ctl show connections
.IP \(bu 2
.B modbus-cache-ctl request flush cache
.IP \(bu 2
.B printf 'show cache\enrequest flush cache\en' | modbus-cache-ctl
.RE

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CTL ", " CONTROL_TOKEN
the control target and the TCP token when the flags are unset.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
every command answered \fBok\fR.
.TP
.B 1
connection or control error.
.TP
.B 2
command-line misuse.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR modbus-cache (1),
.BR modbus-cache-cli (1)
